course: dictionary
lesson: 13646
title: Words that show a beginning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you when something starts. Infancy is one of them. It means the time when someone is a baby or a very young child. «Lily spent her infancy in a small house by the sea.» The clue is the word spent, which tells you about her very first years, when she was a baby.
explain: Infancy can also mean the very early stage of something new, like an idea or an invention. «Space travel is still in its infancy.» Ask yourself: is this about a baby, or about something that has only just started? Here it has only just started, so infancy must mean the early stage.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Space travel is still in its early stage» still makes sense, so you are right. If your meaning does not fit, look at the clues again.
fact: Infancy means the time when someone is a baby or a very young child.
fact: Infancy usually means roughly the first year or two of human life, when babies grow very fast.
fact: «He died in infancy» means he died as a baby, which was common in the past.
fact: Infancy can also mean the very early stage of something new, such as an idea or an invention.
fact: «Space travel is still in its infancy» means it has only just begun.
exercise: «Her infancy was spent in a small village by the sea.» What does infancy mean here? | The time she moved house | *The time she was a baby | The time she went to school | The time she was very old
exercise: «The new phone app is still in its infancy.» What does infancy suggest? | It has been used for a hundred years | It is the best app ever made | *It has only just started | It is broken and should be thrown away
exercise: Find and copy the one word that means the time when someone is a baby: «Grandma has happy memories of her infancy.» | Grandma | memories | *infancy | happy
test: «Many children in the past died in infancy.» What does this mean? | They lived to be very old | *They died as babies | They grew up very quickly | They died at school
test: «The idea for the robot is still in its infancy.» What does this mean? | The robot is finished and sold in shops | The idea is very old | The robot is broken | *The idea has only just begun
exam: «Babies grow very fast during infancy.» Which word is closest in meaning to infancy? | Adulthood | *Early life | Old age | Retirement
